1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Chapter eleven.

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,440
Salah, dhikr and the wandering mind: what the

3
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:07,560
Qur'an and the authentic Sunnah teach, what science

4
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:10,603
has actually tested, and how to use both.

5
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:14,200
A warm-up from the last chapter.

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,840
Why does the moment work gets uncomfortable matter

7
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:17,847
so much?

8
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,180
It is when MD fires, and it is

9
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:27,240
also when effortful practice builds skill.

10
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:30,600
Staying two more minutes protects your focus and

11
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:31,810
builds your craft.

12
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:34,040
Here is the big picture.

13
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:36,140
The Qur'an and the authentic Sunnah treat a

14
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,920
wandering mind as normal, and they prescribe a

15
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,980
precise response: remove the distracting cue, settle the

16
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:46,560
body, do not hold unbidden thoughts against yourself,

17
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:48,480
meet the pull with a brief act of

18
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:51,460
remembrance, and go back to the task.

19
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:54,480
Almost every step matches the psychology you already

20
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:55,221
use.

21
00:00:55,695 --> 00:00:57,820
Science claims carry the same grades as the

22
00:00:57,820 --> 00:01:00,000
rest of your course: A for a randomised

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,620
trial in MD or robust meta-analysis, B for

24
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:06,480
trials in related problems, C for small or

25
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:10,360
correlational studies, and D for untested inference.

26
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:13,333
The texts are graded by source instead: the

27
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:16,280
Qur'an, Bukhari or Muslim, or another collection with

28
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:18,860
a named grading that the major scholars do

29
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:20,160
not dispute.

30
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:22,110
No Sufi sources are used.

31
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,520
Now the honest part.

32
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:26,060
There is no controlled trial of salah and

33
00:01:26,060 --> 00:01:28,420
attention, and no study at all of prayer

34
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:30,670
or dhikr and maladaptive daydreaming.

35
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:34,220
Dhikr has three small studies, all measuring anxiety

36
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:35,770
in hospital patients.

37
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:38,940
Qur'an listening has more, 28 trials in the

38
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:41,490
main review, but all were from one country,

39
00:01:41,490 --> 00:01:45,660
none reported blinding, and they measured short-term anxiety,

40
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:46,631
not focus.

41
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:51,120
In randomised head-to-head trials, Qur'an recitation and music

42
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:55,780
cut anxiety about equally, for example in 238

43
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,680
cancer patients.

44
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:00,180
So much of the short-term calm looks like

45
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:03,360
ordinary relaxation and expectation.

46
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:06,240
Whether devotion adds something more has simply not

47
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,141
been tested.

48
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,740
So what can these practices realistically do for

49
00:02:09,740 --> 00:02:10,260
you?

50
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:12,160
They give your day five fixed cues that

51
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,180
bound work blocks and anchor habits.

52
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:16,180
They give you a ready replacement act for

53
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:18,100
urges and idle time.

54
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,580
They offer short-term calm, but not proven desk

55
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:21,560
focus.

56
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:24,260
They give bedtime, your worst window, a fixed

57
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:25,200
script.

58
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,900
And they offer less guilt about the pull,

59
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:30,060
without permission to follow every fantasy.

60
00:02:30,060 --> 00:02:32,301
They cannot cure MD on their own.

61
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:36,100
The most practical focus texts are about surroundings,

62
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:37,440
not willpower.

63
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:40,160
The Prophet, peace be upon him, sent away

64
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,220
a garment because its markings diverted his attention

65
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:44,620
from the prayer.

66
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:46,840
He had a patterned curtain removed.

67
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,540
He said there is no prayer when food

68
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:51,200
is served, or when nature calls.

69
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,200
And he told the drowsy to sleep first,

70
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:56,260
until they understand what they are saying.

71
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:59,740
That is stimulus control, the same method recommended

72
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:02,440
against music cues in MD.

73
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,160
Moving your earbuds to another room follows the

74
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:07,824
same logic, and admits no weakness.

75
00:03:08,357 --> 00:03:12,180
Bukhari 159 promises great reward for two rak'ahs

76
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:15,000
prayed without thinking of anything else, which can

77
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,100
sound impossible with MD.

78
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:19,540
But Ibn Hajar explains that thoughts and whispers

79
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,720
that rush in, and are hard to repel,

80
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:23,200
are forgiven.

81
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:25,600
What counts is the self-talk the mind runs

82
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,760
along with, and that a person can cut

83
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:28,560
off.

84
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:31,700
He also reports al-Nawawi's view that the reward

85
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:34,307
is still earned despite passing thoughts.

86
00:03:34,829 --> 00:03:37,500
Psychology draws the same line between intentional and

87
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,440
unintentional mind-wandering.

88
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:40,980
So the chain is this.

89
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:43,540
A thought arrives unbidden: that is forgiven, and

90
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:44,120
normal.

91
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,340
Then you notice it.

92
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:47,280
That moment is the decision point.

93
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,020
You either build it into a scene, the

94
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,380
deliberate step MD is made of, or you

95
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:53,200
return to the next phrase.

96
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,640
Even the Prophet, peace be upon him, remembered

97
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:57,760
some gold left at home during the Asr

98
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:58,500
prayer.

99
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,520
He finished the prayer, then went to give

100
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,196
it away.

101
00:04:01,460 --> 00:04:04,160
The texts on whispering say plainly that thoughts

102
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,980
are not deeds.

103
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:07,780
Allah has pardoned this ummah for what their

104
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,880
souls tell them, as long as they do

105
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:12,180
not act on it or speak of it.

106
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:14,820
When some Companions were horrified by their own

107
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:18,320
thoughts, the Prophet, peace be upon him, called

108
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,597
that very distress clear faith.

109
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:22,780
And the response is brief.

110
00:04:22,780 --> 00:04:23,700
Notice it.

111
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,340
Name it as mere whispering.

112
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:28,000
Seek refuge in Allah, and desist.

113
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,200
Ibn Hajar explains desisting as stopping going along

114
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,860
with the thought, and repelling it by occupying

115
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,140
yourself with something else.

116
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:39,260
That is notice, name, return, in the words

117
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,147
of the Sunnah.

118
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,380
Suppression research supports this design.

119
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:44,940
People told not to think of a white

120
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:48,100
bear thought of it more afterwards, and meta-analyses

121
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,400
keep finding that rebound.

122
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:53,460
But people given one specific distracter were less

123
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,260
preoccupied later.

124
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,420
For you, the something else must be the

125
00:04:57,420 --> 00:05:00,720
task itself, not another fantasy, and not an

126
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,683
open-ended spell of worship.

127
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:05,660
The Qur'an calls empty wishing amani.

128
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:08,060
It is not obtained by your wishful thinking,

129
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:11,740
says chapter 4, verse 123.

130
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:15,380
On verse 119, Ibn Kathir spells out what

131
00:05:15,380 --> 00:05:18,960
Shaytan's false hopes contain: making it attractive to

132
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:23,440
abandon repentance, and ordering taswif, which is procrastination

133
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:24,900
and delay.

134
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:28,660
These verses concern salvation, not careers, so the

135
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,680
link to success daydreams is the structure: a

136
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:34,280
wish standing in for a deed, with delay

137
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:35,660
to follow.

138
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:38,520
That is the same structure Oettingen found in

139
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:39,571
her experiments.

140
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:44,320
Muslim 2664 is the Sunnah's most compact text

141
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:46,120
on self-regulation.

142
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,300
Be keen on what benefits you, seek Allah's

143
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:50,260
help, and do not be helpless.

144
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,400
If something befalls you, do not say, if

145
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:54,460
only I had done such and such, but

146
00:05:54,460 --> 00:05:56,900
say, Allah decreed, and what He willed He

147
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:59,020
did, for if opens the door to the

148
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,680
work of Shaytan.

149
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:03,700
Al-Nawawi explains that the warning covers saying it

150
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,137
where it brings no benefit.

151
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:07,760
Read clause by clause, it is WOOP.

152
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,540
Be keen on what benefits you is the

153
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:10,320
wish.

154
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:12,760
Do not be helpless names the inner obstacle:

155
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,640
the moment discomfort makes escape attractive.

156
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:18,180
Seek Allah's help and act is the plan.

157
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:20,860
And after a lapse, Allah decreed replaces if

158
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:23,560
only, which cuts the regret loop.

159
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:25,920
Together with the verses on wishful thinking, the

160
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:29,140
texts close both exits of the wandering mind:

161
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,514
fantasy forward, and regret backward.

162
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:34,080
Idle time is where your daydreams win by

163
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:35,040
default.

164
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:37,440
The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: there

165
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,500
are two blessings that many people are deceived

166
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:42,140
into losing: health and free time.

167
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,280
Ibn Hajar notes that many people means those

168
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:46,500
who succeed here are few, so this struggle

169
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:48,760
is the common human one, not a personal

170
00:06:48,760 --> 00:06:49,220
defect.

171
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:51,700
And the Qur'an says: so when you have

172
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:54,260
finished, then stand up for worship.

173
00:06:54,260 --> 00:06:56,220
That verse has the very shape of an

174
00:06:56,220 --> 00:06:57,251
if-then plan.

175
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,660
The most beloved of deeds to Allah is

176
00:06:59,660 --> 00:07:02,580
the most consistent, even if small.

177
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:04,820
Ibn Hajar reads the command to do what

178
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:06,520
you are able to as choosing deeds you

179
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:09,260
can keep up, and al-Nawawi says the continuous

180
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:12,320
little bears fruit until it exceeds the interrupted

181
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:14,600
much, many times over.

182
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,860
That is habit formation: a small fixed act

183
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:21,025
beats an ambitious start that ends in quitting.

184
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,740
Can recitation replace your music?

185
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:26,260
This part is untested inference.

186
00:07:26,260 --> 00:07:28,860
What made music an amplifier was a steady

187
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:32,200
beat, heroic and status themes, and its role

188
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:35,280
as a learned cue for the ritual.

189
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:38,620
Voice-only recitation has no drum pulse, and points

190
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:40,060
to Allah rather than fame.

191
00:07:40,060 --> 00:07:43,300
But played through headphones while pacing, as phonk

192
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:46,520
was, it can inherit the old ritual.

193
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:49,500
The better swap is behavioural: counted dhikr said

194
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,900
while standing still or back at the desk,

195
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:54,120
or reciting from memory.

196
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:57,891
Which nasheeds are permissible: ask a qualified scholar.

197
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,440
Background recitation while you write is a separate

198
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:01,400
problem.

199
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:04,960
Across 65 studies, intelligible speech and lyrics were

200
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:06,660
the most distracting sounds for reading.

201
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,720
If you understand the Arabic, recitation behind a

202
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,420
script should cost about what song lyrics cost.

203
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:15,100
So silence stays the default for scripting.

204
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,820
It also sidesteps a question of adab: the

205
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:20,160
Qur'an asks that when it is recited, we

206
00:08:20,160 --> 00:08:21,940
listen and pay attention.

207
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:25,160
Whether background recitation fits that: ask a qualified

208
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:25,889
scholar.

209
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:27,660
Now the protocol.

210
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:29,260
Prayer at its time is among the most

211
00:08:29,260 --> 00:08:32,160
beloved deeds, which gives you five external cues

212
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:32,680
a day.

213
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,820
Plan work blocks between prayers.

214
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:37,540
When the adhan goes, save, and write the

215
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:39,500
next ten-minute step on paper.

216
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,180
Make wudu as a reset.

217
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:43,600
After the salam and its adhkar, start that

218
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,820
step before touching your phone.

219
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,840
The hard stretch of an edit now ends

220
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:50,440
at a visible point, which bounds the discomfort

221
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,626
that triggers you.

222
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:54,820
When work turns uncomfortable and the pull starts:

223
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:56,960
notice it, and name it, the pull.

224
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,280
Say one isti'adha, I seek refuge with Allah

225
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:01,600
from Satan, or one short dhikr, once, not

226
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,180
until the pull fades.

227
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:04,880
Then do the next two-minute step of the

228
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:07,420
task, and log the episode that evening.

229
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:09,740
The Qur'an frames it: when an impulse from

230
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:12,400
Satan touches them, they remember, and at once

231
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:13,780
they see clearly.

232
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:16,320
If a success fantasy is running, park it

233
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,747
for your written WOOP slot.

234
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:21,000
Bedtime, your worst window, gets the Sunnah's most

235
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,060
detailed routine, all from Bukhari.

236
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:27,280
After Isha, no idle talk and no screen,

237
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,820
with devices out of the bedroom.

238
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:32,440
In bed, recite Ayat al-Kursi and the last

239
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,580
two verses of al-Baqarah.

240
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:36,920
Blow the three Quls into cupped hands and

241
00:09:36,920 --> 00:09:38,720
wipe them over your body.

242
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:42,700
Say Subhan Allah 33 times, al-hamdu lillah 33,

243
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:44,900
and Allahu akbar 34.

244
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:47,300
Last, on your right side, the dua: O

245
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,560
Allah, I submit myself to You, with the

246
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:52,760
instruction to let these be your last words.

247
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,300
Counted, spoken words may occupy the inner voice

248
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:58,560
that fantasy needs, though that is untested.

249
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:01,060
Say it once, as worship, not over and

250
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:02,784
over until it feels right.

251
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,960
Two risks need guarding.

252
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,920
The first is compulsion.

253
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,460
More than half of people diagnosed with MD

254
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:13,740
had OCD-related disorders, so dhikr or wudu repeated

255
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:17,420
until it feels right can become a ritual.

256
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:20,720
Warning signs are repeating for relief or certainty,

257
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:23,720
restarting prayers, and time creeping up.

258
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:26,120
The Sunnah has its own brakes, like basing

259
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,980
prayer on what you are sure of, and

260
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:30,880
the right help is an ERP-trained clinician working

261
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,920
with a qualified scholar.

262
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:34,840
The second risk is escape.

263
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:36,600
If you leave a hard edit for extra

264
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,320
worship and never come back, worship is doing

265
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,040
the fantasy's job.

266
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:43,400
The test for every act: does it return

267
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:45,560
you to the task, or replace it?

268
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:47,900
Finally, learn like a hafiz.

269
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:51,260
Hifz runs three tracks: sabaq, the new lesson

270
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:54,920
recited without the text; sabqi, recent portions revised

271
00:10:54,920 --> 00:10:59,180
daily; and manzil, older portions in rotation.

272
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,980
That is retrieval and spaced review, the best

273
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:04,020
tools in learning science.

274
00:11:04,020 --> 00:11:07,280
The texts describe the forgetting: memorised Quran runs

275
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:09,420
off like camels set loose.

276
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:11,660
Use the model for your craft: one new

277
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:14,840
hook technique a day, last week's reviewed daily,

278
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,580
older skills in rotation, each tested by doing.

279
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,500
Don't expect a bigger memory, though.

280
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,835
Huffaz show none, only the skill they rehearse.

281
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,200
The most useful thing the texts add is

282
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:29,500
a stance: the unbidden thought carries no guilt,

283
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,160
while following it is a choice you can

284
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,720
still reverse at the moment of noticing.

285
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:36,840
Mercy about the pull, accountability for the scene.

286
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:39,170
Nobody has tested whether any of this changes

287
00:11:39,170 --> 00:11:42,040
MD, so the honest line is consistent with

288
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,600
the science, not proven by it.

289
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:47,540
Your daily log, comparing days with and without

290
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:50,060
the anchors, is the only evidence there will

291
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:50,510
be.

292
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:53,940
According to Ibn Hajar, which thoughts in prayer

293
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:56,855
are forgiven, and which part is the choice?

294
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:04,140
Thoughts that rush in unbidden are forgiven.

295
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,540
Running along with them is the choice.

296
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:09,516
The decision point is the moment you notice.

297
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:11,840
What is the test for any act of

298
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:14,218
worship you use in an urge moment?

299
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,220
Does it return you to the task, or

300
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:21,420
replace it?

301
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:24,063
One act, once, then back to the work.

